#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render a firmware review findings.json into report.html, report.md and findings.csv.

Usage: render_report.py <findings.json> [--out-dir DIR] [--open]

Validates the JSON first; exits 1 with a list of problems if it is invalid.
With --open, launches report.html in the default browser once it is written
(macOS, Windows and Linux), unless the run looks headless: a CI environment
(CI, GITHUB_ACTIONS, GITLAB_CI, JENKINS_URL, TF_BUILD, BUILDKITE, CIRCLECI,
TEAMCITY_VERSION), no display on Linux, or an SSH session. In that case
it prints why it skipped and exits 0. Override with the environment variable
FW_REVIEW_OPEN=0 (never open) or FW_REVIEW_OPEN=1 / --force-open (open even
when CI is detected). A failure to open never fails the render: the files are
already on disk, so the script prints the file:// path instead and exits 0.
"""
